# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# WITHOUT this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore — and a release package
# unpacked from the ZIP has no .gitignore and no .git at all. INSTALL.md tells
# the installer to run `npm ci` before seeding demo data, so the fallback would
# then upload the entire node_modules tree on the next ./scripts/deploy.sh.
#
# Being explicit also means a developer checkout and a customer's installation
# upload byte-for-byte the same build context.
#
# This is NOT .dockerignore. This decides what leaves the machine; .dockerignore
# decides what docker then sees. tests/ and scripts/ must survive BOTH, because
# the `tester` stage typechecks and runs the suite inside the image.

.git/
.gcloudignore

node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
coverage/

# Never upload an installation's own configuration or anyone's credentials.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
.deploy.env
serviceAccount*.json

.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
*-debug.log

__pycache__/
*.pyc

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.tsbuildinfo
